#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092021 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "aebe3048-cc5b-5340-a15e-d577ae2ee72a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5479" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/901d3a22065b48a8076b9c9aae5563c770c36c9ad40e4063c0f739847e1cda98.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/0c6f9f860a1cf4d510f6c3d4d9c66b77496a354bb1e2cef1b69fd1178e4f15ab.png)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "55e695b2-4581-5ba7-9604-506234b88323" :question/math-academy-id "e-5480" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/5ca3e07cfbe9e5d4956b1eab4393601f2a78b0b067d17312e71cbac993e28a86.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/fdbcc62870aefab6214b2f24f53e9bc5654e5386639d4bc328dff3769aff2b45.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092023 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "a42d0af8-869c-5c2a-8182-22b14b9546e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5481" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/a1b88b7897649bb059cef39d40b2b052a13ac28282223b5688a1bce98296fb53.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/ca8f02e390e338b62956302ec45ea274ad73a51dafde3fe93b3d1e37dd663699.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9e40836e-18e9-5df6-a930-05875b920335" :question/math-academy-id "e-5482" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/603c59d43e3be000931e7279ac4d27be8aa92692f1528ec57ebd52172affa3cb.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/f91e4886c58db10f60fa666a870aed3c2f456b25e6afb560f857e9c36e81217c.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/aa89b93c6fabd2f3dc7063c85e253ded7482018a5f1c6dadedc74964194c5754.png)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dfc28bf-3507-580f-9a32-880486bbb48f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda +6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359172} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3901f6-4bdd-5862-ba21-95fbde66c0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359173} {:answer/id #uuid "3351d9d5-d4ce-5bca-8384-479ec5902fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359174} {:answer/id #uuid "90f78ee3-5e94-53b5-a4e0-3933d4c94378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359175} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1757e3-9f2f-5ed9-aa46-29b070e147b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda -5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90f78ee3-5e94-53b5-a4e0-3933d4c94378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359175} :answer-field/id #uuid "4027fe01-8dd0-5bb3-a081-dcda06ceda50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "800018b3-d1f0-57dc-9733-5d56dae63cca" :question/math-academy-id "q-106958" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ 5-5\\lambda -\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+0 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e19d340-4e62-5539-a202-5a5a4a57f54d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359179} {:answer/id #uuid "147220da-5f19-590c-8df0-44c3d8c97c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359180} {:answer/id #uuid "e69c2b94-fd5a-5956-a0e8-60a8e558dfe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359181} {:answer/id #uuid "ede9ca59-93a1-58d5-86b4-008dff9bd072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359182} {:answer/id #uuid "fed3e408-fea6-5fee-923d-31d95f4d7b30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ede9ca59-93a1-58d5-86b4-008dff9bd072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359182} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b09a31-18bf-51a8-9be4-1317c9f48324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "68216f82-a312-524f-becc-2374f6ca189d" :question/math-academy-id "q-106995" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =3.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e502208-a850-5d05-bd93-d293a8fba1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =23$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359186} {:answer/id #uuid "2c71b747-e1a3-5f44-8110-e8b2787fe728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-8$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359187} {:answer/id #uuid "55ed2e2f-d6c8-5e81-9916-fa53d876d6ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359188} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcdab46-6c64-5a2d-a2e6-8b7093dfb048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359189} {:answer/id #uuid "38844d2f-6851-5e63-a2eb-cf86b5db0b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdcdab46-6c64-5a2d-a2e6-8b7093dfb048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359189} :answer-field/id #uuid "658127fa-7d23-57c7-a3c1-ca26136930a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bc4edb2-a90d-543d-9659-c11413861acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-106999" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}23 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}23-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}23-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (23-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-8) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -23) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =23.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c537cc6-c052-57a9-b158-9535769d7f82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =9$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359193} {:answer/id #uuid "83fe7cc5-7e75-5083-b3f3-0b95a9410ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359194} {:answer/id #uuid "b841752f-674d-5945-bb07-dd40bba48a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359195} {:answer/id #uuid "072c591e-a145-51dc-afa1-48e0f3783e40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359196} {:answer/id #uuid "65e90b5e-b386-5128-b61b-1376151666ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65e90b5e-b386-5128-b61b-1376151666ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359197} :answer-field/id #uuid "85eed561-2f89-5991-807b-64207407a17e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "516deea5-c1fd-59bf-8d83-57450943e342" :question/math-academy-id "q-107843" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}18 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}18-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}18-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (18-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -18) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d25d95a8-9dc9-5ea3-8c14-ca55a38c4923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =43$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359200} {:answer/id #uuid "2e864fa6-2716-5653-b992-c76d1389180e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =13$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359201} {:answer/id #uuid "5c8bd375-ddcb-54f2-aaf0-bac3bedcf3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =43$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359202} {:answer/id #uuid "e003cfaa-e3b2-525f-9b4c-da1299d2fd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =13$ and $\\lambda =43$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359203} {:answer/id #uuid "c5354561-6919-52db-b304-546938528e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5354561-6919-52db-b304-546938528e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359204} :answer-field/id #uuid "901f9a2b-e84a-5333-b611-b0d558fe65e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2684b28-0c59-5171-ade6-34093aeb8db7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107852" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ 40-5\\lambda -8\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +43 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-13)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 43 \\\\  & =169-172 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a29d2e12-b11b-5686-8940-176e5834c784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359207} {:answer/id #uuid "26768d28-bc66-5458-9e7a-d74fa51bdb21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359208} {:answer/id #uuid "80b647d1-0fa4-549d-890c-974defa2f7f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359209} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e57cdc-54a7-5f29-898f-98baa1199eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359210} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9b0db0-02bd-5995-9e4e-0c406e15dd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80b647d1-0fa4-549d-890c-974defa2f7f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359209} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ab3dcf-b07b-535c-8382-017b67889e19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c33673b-c006-5cdb-9984-8678f994e9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-107987" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-6\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ -40-8\\lambda +5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cbcb05c-0d49-5cbd-80eb-6b804f107249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = \\sqrt{3}$ and $λ = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089209} {:answer/id #uuid "0a494e60-093c-58c4-a59c-aa2a3b60e7e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089210} {:answer/id #uuid "323c248b-e18e-5611-b08d-9631fd900654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $λ = \\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089211} {:answer/id #uuid "479da784-7457-5ebe-ab3e-66bcab6eacf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $λ =-\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089212} {:answer/id #uuid "5016ca94-d6c8-5940-9a53-df997f015259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbcb05c-0d49-5cbd-80eb-6b804f107249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = \\sqrt{3}$ and $λ = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089209} :answer-field/id #uuid "aed5cf4f-5cf4-5caf-81e8-f22caef29322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1fb4b20-223a-5224-b15e-06a76416065c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11983" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c8c43de-912c-5dad-8e48-9667a7b11751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359214} {:answer/id #uuid "49ec8ad1-065e-51a6-a846-2f365deaa67d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359215} {:answer/id #uuid "214ce70a-010d-547a-ab86-537ebe7bdff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-9$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359216} {:answer/id #uuid "47cb7ae8-f9eb-5ead-be15-1a9092917aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359217} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a89384-dc03-5237-81f4-b8b289a1137e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3a89384-dc03-5237-81f4-b8b289a1137e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359218} :answer-field/id #uuid "4895cbac-a255-5291-8c8f-7cffa35698d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d077ff2-3486-5e52-9751-5d43b56206bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-11984" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $M-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nM-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(M-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 16+4\\lambda +4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda -9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 9}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 10}{2} \\\\  & =1,-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "958eb313-8eb6-5031-a652-a4e5dd9925fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294526} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2c98c8-dde6-5160-860d-95f972eed39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$  (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294527} {:answer/id #uuid "86c421c8-23b5-5b82-9614-79651e5ebf72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294528} {:answer/id #uuid "1199a2e1-6452-5f3c-adbc-e5506a0a9b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294529} {:answer/id #uuid "b625c85e-ad5b-5b27-99e8-54f4d0d6d292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b625c85e-ad5b-5b27-99e8-54f4d0d6d292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294530} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1d8f83f-93a5-5a9a-bb8f-efe63bf1e4f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a59a38-6b0a-5bff-ab4c-adc26ea6a0e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-12296" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $S-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nS-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-8-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(S-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-8-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-8-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ -32+8\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{64}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 8}{2} \\\\  & =-6,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaff2f96-5d6d-553b-87e8-7d5f59285d98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359221} {:answer/id #uuid "4692e5d7-4a64-5967-8316-02b23932ccf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359222} {:answer/id #uuid "656255ab-343c-5956-a970-7e734ee8bffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359223} {:answer/id #uuid "024144e9-03a4-5eaf-aec2-a5cdb989826a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359224} {:answer/id #uuid "b12461b4-8ced-56da-8e26-7ca5a2f85355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4692e5d7-4a64-5967-8316-02b23932ccf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359222} :answer-field/id #uuid "32ac2b1a-190d-533a-8d29-9a1cc912d26e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd21fd58-7abf-54bb-add3-4da127deb87b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36756" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 \\\\ 16 & 12\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ 16 & 12-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ 16 & 12-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-4-\\lambda )(12-\\lambda )-16\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -48+4\\lambda -12\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda =4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee9bc6f-5a72-5add-8ecc-1b71282a0419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} - 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090282} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d2940b-62bd-566f-a82a-fd40ff14c2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} + 4λ + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090283} {:answer/id #uuid "175f4c67-f0a6-5f3f-b81c-431534fbf93d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} - 4λ - 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090284} {:answer/id #uuid "57b0c675-56c8-59fd-a95d-6833904978ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} - 4λ + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090285} {:answer/id #uuid "6221c02d-d3ab-509e-9bb6-056de1d0571f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} + 3λ + 9 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9d2940b-62bd-566f-a82a-fd40ff14c2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} + 4λ + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090283} :answer-field/id #uuid "f641e017-3fcd-5a0a-a1e7-e9e7601b5fca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21a76447-bb7c-5d72-a771-38739632e899" :question/math-academy-id "q-36758" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )-(-8)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -12-2\\lambda +6\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "577d4d32-d140-5e81-aa29-e46aa6dfde51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359228} {:answer/id #uuid "842fa6f6-d993-5bc1-957b-639750bcd703" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359229} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4d1cb8-9b59-5e53-b5b1-894ef4d3df5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359230} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbaf891-3cd8-55dd-a78f-1a5548b21e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda +2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359231} {:answer/id #uuid "6d09329f-8403-57f5-9d19-c8690f6e0bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "577d4d32-d140-5e81-aa29-e46aa6dfde51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359228} :answer-field/id #uuid "41049a2c-fc94-5a81-821d-1b6d4e8e3d06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "677d9a3d-176b-51d5-bf00-dfe19a876531" :question/math-academy-id "q-36771" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$D=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 4 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 4 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )-(-5)\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ -35-5\\lambda +7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -15 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af44a87e-26da-5096-85ff-780ae0baf3eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 8$ and $λ = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090294} {:answer/id #uuid "d645007a-712e-567d-9277-c4aa59d7d840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 8$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090295} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6f39b7-0975-5673-b988-9d3fd267b722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-6$ and $λ =-10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090296} {:answer/id #uuid "20eefca5-71cc-5e10-82b4-6391ca5fba54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090297} {:answer/id #uuid "232e2323-0dca-511f-8115-f44c3edf1827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 6$ and $λ = 10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20eefca5-71cc-5e10-82b4-6391ca5fba54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090297} :answer-field/id #uuid "40774c4b-45e1-57e2-b84f-15814ca61892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f563abe4-0d8d-5d69-9a75-20dcd9079f0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36776" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-6-\\lambda )(-10-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 60+6\\lambda +10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16\\lambda +66 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={16}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =256-264 \\\\  & =-8 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions, and therefore, $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ee4662-bb53-5d74-8309-dbedd4a9ef42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359235} {:answer/id #uuid "ca034c8a-7b28-56cf-ab40-578a22b15610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359236} {:answer/id #uuid "afe3c234-4e11-53c6-87d4-16c32c787dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$  (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359237} {:answer/id #uuid "9d85bcbe-a76b-5262-81ff-7872bd626617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359238} {:answer/id #uuid "b3bbd308-5322-5518-9e15-2babb35954b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe3c234-4e11-53c6-87d4-16c32c787dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$  (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359237} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c1a0966-4032-53f1-a39e-b9b2aa22c11d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b14bc23-f539-5c26-97da-0a4a4fc1772d" :question/math-academy-id "q-36778" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(E-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )-(-2)\\cdot 8 & =0 \\\\ -12-2\\lambda +6\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $E$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3826d89a-2af6-52c5-a6f2-b8ecee0417ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359242} {:answer/id #uuid "1e338e05-88b3-56bf-86d1-4379ce4359d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359243} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a1c470-a33a-5cb6-86a2-68dde0c627ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359244} {:answer/id #uuid "16e9d546-0fa2-512e-acdd-cd6b67cb5fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359245} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd4247c-edb9-5741-9332-7f630ddb11f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0a1c470-a33a-5cb6-86a2-68dde0c627ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359244} :answer-field/id #uuid "e79ad3c6-64db-56e9-b86a-2b6c0ddbff9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fda33b2-0f78-5ef6-abce-da9e465c13f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36780" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84358367-d455-5ca7-9587-e0b7e7d302fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359249} {:answer/id #uuid "cabae2fc-73ef-5ec6-9d49-453d56492414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359250} {:answer/id #uuid "59ae3007-ef7a-5674-97df-eeb9d09a8b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359251} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e3f0c1-f191-5b95-bc0d-239995b11e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359252} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c104da-342b-5f2b-ab52-a4beec3beb81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7e3f0c1-f191-5b95-bc0d-239995b11e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359252} :answer-field/id #uuid "25c90e1f-35c1-5054-abba-972b0e7a0bca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b71cd1e-e595-5b69-93e4-b971cfae835c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76343" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $N=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 2+2\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd7e612d-504c-5b59-843d-09f92ad6a2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359256} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4938dd-735e-5f49-b85c-07c48a5d7804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =6$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359257} {:answer/id #uuid "d7af984b-e477-55e0-b830-64a4b5f50058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359258} {:answer/id #uuid "92c807b7-297c-5415-bd71-dc877203d1ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\sqrt{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359259} {:answer/id #uuid "1779872a-632b-5cb9-843b-554ea3bf75c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd7e612d-504c-5b59-843d-09f92ad6a2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359256} :answer-field/id #uuid "604dcb0f-2420-5377-8324-04c58a13063a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a400aa29-b613-5c26-88d6-532019155a9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76364" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +\\sqrt{7}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459edef4-96b4-55a8-8e73-679dac580a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359263} {:answer/id #uuid "15628db6-2338-565d-947f-76ea47a954e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359264} {:answer/id #uuid "68f6bd85-6537-5249-9662-e1813e3815ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359265} {:answer/id #uuid "33bc9a22-8541-548e-9a24-7df412c862f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359266} {:answer/id #uuid "e494d672-1480-59a0-a224-1c54edb768e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "459edef4-96b4-55a8-8e73-679dac580a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359263} :answer-field/id #uuid "736ecb9a-3a65-5324-97c7-56c15235347f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ac77f13-6e66-5a66-832a-a4511ee2597c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9340" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-7\\cdot 7 & =0 \\\\ 4-2\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -45 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 45}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 14}{2} \\\\  & =-5,9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fca4302-bc01-5c13-b05e-6a6d53aa05de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359270} {:answer/id #uuid "31bcde44-13fd-5e95-a560-dcde98b97aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359271} {:answer/id #uuid "02d63f4c-60c6-58b4-bd94-03553d986b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359272} {:answer/id #uuid "61265773-2e56-57f4-a08d-ecc24c68d8b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359273} {:answer/id #uuid "d33e59de-afb9-5c3d-9b6b-7e2c081c732b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fca4302-bc01-5c13-b05e-6a6d53aa05de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359270} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a3442a-c80e-510f-a9ee-1f5d6ef25475" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33ca03a0-a8c8-587c-a9fa-20692dfe790c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9347" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(D-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 9-3\\lambda -3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =5,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df390032-d3b7-55db-87d1-0f0aae330281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359277} {:answer/id #uuid "03479e59-dc74-5b3b-a0c5-99d68ccd5c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359278} {:answer/id #uuid "31d19957-3a77-5909-9179-f5877e8d7544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359279} {:answer/id #uuid "9122f78f-fbce-5ce3-8be4-f81cad2854f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359280} {:answer/id #uuid "87ff88bc-a960-5336-bd4c-dd6aa8f203e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d19957-3a77-5909-9179-f5877e8d7544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359279} :answer-field/id #uuid "363ad05a-ee9d-57eb-b5ff-cf6835e90a77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ef000ed-46a1-5b2b-a4bc-fcc72b57d4f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-9348" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -2+\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4.$"}]}
